prompt:
For the metric described as collective carbon emissions reduction, extract any reported actual value.

CLAIMS:
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_052", "text": "Alphabet has an aspiration to help individuals, cities, and other partners collectively reduce 1 gigaton of carbon equivalent emissions annually by 2030."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_073", "text": "Optimizations to Google's standard data center design collectively have the potential to reduce the embodied carbon emissions intensity of a data center building by around 9%."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_092", "text": "Alphabet reports emissions in metric tons per gas and in metric tons of carbon dioxide equivalent (tCO2e), with biogenic emissions reported as tCO2 only."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_134", "text": "Alphabet uses a 25-year estimated lifespan for solar panels in both annual and lifetime emissions reduction methods."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_135", "text": "The estimated annual enabled emissions reduction takes into account solar installations enabled by Solar API prior to 2024, dating back to 2022, to calculate the total impact in 2024 alone."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_138", "text": "To estimate operational emissions from electricity consumption of running workloads, Google used a one-month sample of observed machine power data from its entire TPU fleet, applying Google's 2023 average fleetwide carbon intensity."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_140", "text": "Data center construction emissions were estimated based on Google's disclosed 2023 carbon footprint."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_001", "text": "Google reduced data center energy emissions by 12% in 2024."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_016", "text": "In 2024, Alphabet reduced its data center energy emissions by 12% compared to 2023."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_045", "text": "In one trial consisting of 70 test flights, flights that adjusted their routes using AI-based contrail predictions showed a 54% reduction in contrail kilometers, compared to control flights."}

Output ONLY: [{"claim_id": "...", "value": number, "unit": "...", "year": number}].
Only include values the company reports as achieved, not targets. Return [] if none.
